Pretraining the Base GPT Model
The model is first trained on this massive dataset to learn:

language patterns,
reasoning,
grammar,
facts,
and contextual understanding.


Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT)
After pretraining, the model undergoes SFT (Supervised Fine-Tuning) using high-quality human-written examples.

Structure:

Request/Input: conversation history or user prompt
Response/Output: the best ideal response written by humans

The goal is to teach the model how an ideal assistant should respond.

Flow:
Base GPT Model → SFT GPT Model

This produces the Base GPT Model.

RLHF (Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback)
In Stage 3, RLHF is applied to further improve response quality.

Human evaluators rank multiple responses generated by the model based on:

helpfulness,
accuracy,
safety,
clarity,
and overall quality.

Reward Model & Ranking System
These rankings are used to train a reward model that predicts which response is better.

The system works probabilistically:

higher probability/score → better response
lower probability/score → weaker response

This process often involves:

binary classification
and optimization using Binary Cross-Entropy (BCE) loss.
















